---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'What to Do Immediately After a Pipe Burst | Water Damage Tips';
const description = 'Practical steps to take right after a pipe bursts in your Ellicott City or Westminster area home to limit damage while waiting for help.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="py-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <nav class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-primary">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-primary">Blog</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span>What to Do After a Pipe Burst</span>
      </nav>
      
      <header class="mb-8">
        <time class="text-sm text-neutral-500" datetime="2025-09-12">September 12, 2025</time>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-neutral-900 mt-2 mb-4">What to Do Immediately After a Pipe Burst</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed">A sudden pipe burst can release a surprising volume of water in a short time. Acting quickly and safely helps limit the damage while professional help is on the way.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none space-y-6 text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">1. Stop the Water if You Can</h2>
        <p>If it is safe to do so, shut off the main water valve to your home. Knowing where this valve is ahead of time saves precious minutes. If the break is isolated to a single fixture, the local shutoff for that fixture may be enough.</p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">2. Protect Yourself and Others</h2>
        <p>Stay away from standing water if electrical outlets or appliances are nearby. Turn off electricity to affected areas at the breaker panel only if you can do so without stepping in water. Keep children and pets clear of the area.</p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">3. Move Belongings Out of Harm’s Way</h2>
        <p>If water is still rising or spreading, move furniture, electronics, and valuables to a dry area when it is safe. Place aluminum foil or plastic under furniture legs that must stay in place to reduce staining of floors and furniture.</p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">4. Call for Professional Help</h2>
        <p>Contact a water damage restoration team as soon as the immediate safety steps are handled. The sooner extraction and drying begin, the lower the risk of secondary damage such as swelling, warping, or mold growth.</p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">5. Document What You Can</h2>
        <p>Take photos or short videos of the affected areas before major cleanup begins. This documentation can be useful for insurance purposes. Note the time you discovered the problem and any actions you took.</p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900">What Not to Do</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>Do not use a regular household vacuum on standing water.</li>
          <li>Avoid turning on HVAC systems that may spread moist air or contaminants.</li>
          <li>Do not assume the problem is solved once visible water is gone—hidden moisture often remains.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="bg-neutral-50 p-6 rounded-xl border border-neutral-100 mt-8">
          If you are dealing with a pipe burst in the Ellicott City, Westminster, or surrounding area, we are available to help with extraction, drying, and restoration. Call <a href="tel:+14105550199" class="text-primary font-semibold">(410) 555-0199</a> for assistance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
